# <type>(<scope>): <summary in English, imperative, no final period>
#
# <body: what and why, wrap at 72 columns>
#
# Closes #<issue>
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Types (only these three), by branch, and how they bump the version:
#   feat      feature/<n>-slug   new feature   -> 1.1.0 -> 1.2.0
#   fix       bug/<n>-slug       bug fix       -> 1.1.0 -> 1.1.1
#   chore     tech/<n>-slug      technical     -> no new version, not in the CHANGELOG
#   feat!     breaking change (or footer "BREAKING CHANGE: ...") -> 2.0.0
#
# Scope (optional): core, search, ui, map, options, api, data, providers,
#   locales, ci...
#
# Issue references (#12) only in the footer, never in the body: commitlint
# takes a body line with one for the start of the footer (a warning, and
# warnings fail like errors).
#
# Issue footer (GitHub closes the issue when this reaches main):
#   Closes #12    Fixes #12    Resolves #12    Refs #12 (does not close)
#
# Lines starting with # are ignored.
